 \"X\" next to item)**\r\n\r\n[ ] Documentation update\r\n[X] Bug fix ([template](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/eslint/eslint/master/templates/bug-report.md))\r\n[ ] New rule ([template](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/eslint/eslint/master/templates/rule-proposal.md))\r\n[ ] Changes an existing rule ([template](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/eslint/eslint/master/templates/rule-change-proposal.md))\r\n[ ] Add autofixing to a rule\r\n[ ] Add a CLI option\r\n[ ] Add something to the core\r\n[ ] Other, please explain:\r\n\r\nFixes https://github.com/eslint/eslint/issues/7538\r\n\r\n**What changes did you make? (Give an overview)**\r\nFixes the curly rule under the \"multi-or-nest\" setting, includes tests, and updates docs with an example\r\n\r\n**Is there anything you'd like reviewers to focus on?**\r\nThis only addresses leading comments and not trailing comments, but I think trailing comment is a bit different because the intent is more ambiguous. For example:\r\n\r\n```js\r\nif (foo)\r\n  baz();\r\n  // line of comment\r\nbar();\r\n```\r\n\r\nIt's unclear if the comment is describing the line above or mis-indented and describing the line below. In my experience, intentional trailing comments are rare.\r\n\r\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eslint/eslint/issues/7539/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eslint/eslint/issues/7539/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}},"event":"cross-referenced"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eslint/eslint/issues/comments/258594368","html_url":"https://github.com/eslint/eslint/issues/7538#issuecomment-258594368","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eslint/eslint/issues/7538","id":258594368,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI1ODU5NDM2OA==","user":{"login":"mysticatea","id":1937871,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5Mzc4NzE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.co